<title>POLAND: Polish broad money falls 0.3 pct in Jan 1-10- NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money falls 0.3 pct in Jan 1-10- NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money fell 414.6 million zlotys, or 0.3 percent, in the January 1-10 period to 135.07 billion after a 5.1- percent jump in all of December, preliminary central bank figures showed.  </p>
<p>BROAD POLISH MONEY		   JAN 1-10   DEC 96	JAN 96</p>
<p>  Change vs pvs period (pct)	  -0.3    5.9(5.1)	 1.1</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		  135.07 135.49(134.49) 105.46</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)    23.32   23.36	    21.44</p>
<p>  National currency		   111.75  112.12(111.12)  84.02</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		  23.79   23.56	    19.28</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector  80.94   81.09(80.24)   56.98</p>
<p>NOTE: revised figures in brackets.</p>
<p>Polish central bank announcement:</p>
<p>From January 1, 1997 the National Bank of Poland introduced changes in methods of monetary aggregate calculation to match standards of international financial institutions. Therefore, December data will be verified after the bank receives commercial banks' balance sheet information.</p>
<p>A full explanation of the introduced changes will be published soon.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
